<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly softer.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly softer.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly softer in all maturities, with only the six-month rate steady, traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A dealer said the lower domestic interest rates mirrored the ample peso liquidity, prodding many banks to lower their swap rates.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks are willing to swap their pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  OCT 29		 OCT 28</p>
<p>    1 W		11  3/16		11  1/4</p>
<p>    2 W		11  3/16		11  1/4</p>
<p>    1 M		11  1/8		 11  1/4</p>
<p>    2 M		11  1/4		 11  5/16</p>
<p>    3 M		11  3/8		 11  7/16</p>
<p>    6 M		11 11/16		11 11/16</p>
<p>    12M		11  3/4		 11 13/16</p>
<p>    VAL		30-Oct		  29-Oct</p>
<p>- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
